NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/config.Config#FirstTurnRelevancePush kind=field
  digest=b3:86c50068b22b8d5a2c7da2a0cf36c0b286b96ca521fdec3f12e1c5e080110431 file=neo/internal/config/config.go range=91:99 lang=go exported=true byte_range=4870:5528
  sig=bool
  doc=FirstTurnRelevancePush injects a bounded RELEVANCE retrieval into the\nactivation window on the FIRST turn of a conversation only. cortex.Activate's\npushed tiers (Pinned/Timeline/Recent) are recency-based and query-INDEPENDENT\n(activate.go: the query arg is unused), so on the opening message the agent\ncarries recency but NOT relevance-to-the-ask unless it reactively calls\nmemory_recall. With this on, Neo runs pager.Retrieve(query) once on turn 1\nand injects the hits, so the opening turn has relevance-matched memory with\nno reactive tool call. After turn 1 the pull-not-push philosophy resumes.
EDGES
  ^contains=matrix/neo/internal/config.Config

